      "text": "/skill:tidy-recipe-authoring\n\nCreate tidy recipes for workbook `0c219894c7243ecbc4eb3b35917ccdb74205fa69c147d1b91453030037df7ef9--prisoners-australia-2006-cube-21-source.xlsx`.\n\n- Publication: Prisoners in Australia (Australian Bureau of Statistics)\n- Release or year: 2006\n- Sheets needing a recipe: 5 of 5\n\n| sheet | sheet_sha256 | current recipe |\n|---|---|---|\n| \"Table 1\" | ed5052d96d09ed4e6c0bf37db8732a5555f0c8eed93f0b06a9acd1cd73e7de9c | missing |\n| \"Table 2\" | 5143c59aeeb8edf81f7f39264f9b96e56d79e4c7e4b79fe42c468c82a4f8b053 | missing |\n| \"Table 3\" | 6466a7a4a7bec07d3981b186c94f6859d217dd47cdc79b44e7f819e6e8114913 | missing |\n| \"Table 4\" | ab683b5d728dd63de695955347c393134af0670eb8c900a9f76e3692cf67b977 | missing |\n| \"Table 5\" | 03480ec28041fae92a2327afac8d5c4b95a895e555fd1e33197970ebd1e25800 | missing |\n\nRelated workbooks:\n- None\n\nWork through every sheet listed above using the skill's workflow. Use\n`codemode` scripts to call the recipe tools, and batch the work: for example,\nlist the workbook and check templates for all sheets in one script, then read\ngrids and test recipes a few sheets at a time. Keep script output short.\n\nName dimensions from `dictionary/dimensions.csv` (see the skill's\n`references/naming.md`); declare any name it lacks in `new_dimensions`.\n\nWrite each recipe to `tidy-recipes/<sheet_sha256>.json` and finish every sheet\nwith `submit_recipe`. You may only write recipe files for this workbook.\n\nEnd with one line per sheet: `sheet | kind | status | records | remaining failures`."
